.TH CBMAP_INSERT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_insert \- insert a key-value pair (type-safe)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cbstmap.h>

cbmap_insert(hm_name, key, val);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-safe wrapper for cbmap_insert_elem() that automatically handles
type conversion and cmap_pair creation. If the key already exists the
value is updated silently. Calls fatal_err() only on a true failure
(i.e. ccol_not_enough_memory or ccol_container_full).
Tree is automatically rebalanced after insertion.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name  BST map to insert into
key      Key to insert
val      Value to associate with key
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Automatically takes address of key and value
Handles both value types and string types correctly
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_insert_elem (3),
.BR cbmap_get (3),
.BR cbmap_remove (3)
